N,N-diethyl-m-toluamide (DEET), and kobs values were compared.
Figure 4-6 shows the results. When photon energy emitted per unit time was plotted
against ln([C]/[C]0), benzoic acid, nitrobenzene, and 1,4-dioxane all showed clearly poorer
degradation at Cl2/N molar = 2 than at 2.5 or 3. All six pollutants had larger kobs values at
Cl2/N molar = 3.
At Cl2/N molar = 3, the kobs values for benzoic acid, nitrobenzene, CBZ, caeeine, 1,4
