kobs values and therefore poorer removal. A possible reason is that these three pollutants
have lower reactivity with the •ClO and •Cl2- radicals generated during breakpoint
chlorination. This interpretation is supported by the reported rate constants for reactions of
the pollutants with •OH, •Cl, •ClO, and •Cl2-.
