chlorine-to-nitrogen ratios with 8 W UVC254 nm/H2O2 showed that although H2O2 can
generate large amounts of •OH and all six pollutants are highly reactive toward •OH,
increasing Cl2/N molar from 2 to 2.5 or 3 substantially improved pollutant degradation and
could exceed removal by 8 W UVC254 nm/H2O2.
